Make the dead Dark One an unique arch-lich - 5d6 cold attack, standard
arch-lich resistances and ten extra levels, on top of his current
abilities, making him slightly more dangerous than the standard
arch-lich - and treat other spellcasting human uniques similarly.
(After all, they'll have had as long to prepare for the rematch as
the player.)

The non-spellcasting human uniques can become vampires instead,
adding a level-drain attack and vampire resistances (including
extra magic resistance) to their current abilities.

The living non-humans - the chromatic dragon, the cyclops, Ixoth,
Scorpius, and Surtur - would become powerful unique zombies in much
the same way.

The two demonic quest nemesis would only gain a few levels.

In practice, what would happen is that the unique would be
killed and the corresponding undead unique marked for creation
in the VotD. It would be impossible to get the undead
versions any other way.

Non-unique humans, such as priests and shopkeepers, would become
produce liches or vampire lords of the same name instead.

Whether this rule applies to the wand of banishment or of death
it would mean using that wand in the main dungeon ends a fight
for now at the cost of making the VotD harder - a fair exchange.

